{
    "name": "change-atlas",
    "title": "Change Atlas",
    "description": "Change Atlas: Pi maps a pull request, branch, commit range, or local changes into an interactive visual report. It reads a git repository (the session's folder, or the folder that Pi names) with `git` (for a pull request also `gh` and `git fetch`, which contact GitHub), and writes reports and fetched PR commits to `change-atlas/` in the data folder. Diff excerpts go to the model provider, and a published report goes to everyone who sees the session. It sends nothing to any other host.",
